.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-transactions - Transactions across every account, or only the stuck ones


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin transactions [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List transactions across every account, each with the payment it belongs to.

.PP
--stuck keeps the ones that need attention: 'unbroadcast' (signed, never sent to the
chain), 'unconfirmed' (sent, never confirmed) or 'any'. --hash finds the transaction an
explorer link or a merchant's message names. A stuck broadcast is re-sent with
\&'rail0 payments redrive  \&' (in write mode, for an operator).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	Only transactions on payments whose payee is one of this account's wallets (account id)

.PP
\fB--chain\fP=
	Only transactions on this chain: a slug (arc, base, …) or a chain id; the environment's gateway decides testnet vs mainnet

.PP
\fB--hash\fP=""
	The transaction with this hash (0x + 64 hex)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for transactions

.PP
\fB--operation\fP=""
	Filter by operation: authorize, capture, charge, void, release, refund, …

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields (prefix - for descending, comma-separated), e.g. -created_at

.PP
\fB--status\fP=[]
	Filter by status (comma-separated or repeated): pending, submitting, submitted, confirmed, failed

.PP
\fB--stuck\fP=""
	Only stuck transactions: unbroadcast, unconfirmed or any


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin transactions --stuck any
  rail0 admin transactions --hash 0xed7c607d…
  rail0 admin transactions --account 019e748b-… --status failed --chain arc
  rail0 admin transactions --operation refund --sort -created_at --pretty
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP
